I wrote `/app/bin/summarize.py` and ran it on `/app/data`, and the output is saved as `/app/out/summary.json`. `/app/tools/check_summary.py` reports that every value matches the reference figures.

The checker only covers `/app/data`, so I haven't tested the script on other exports. I wrote it from the documented rules rather than from what the current files contain. It handles:
- all eight depot formats;
- gzip files, byte order marks and `# charset` directives;
- directives and header rows that change part way through a file;
- rows that carry their own weight unit;
- ISO times with a UTC offset;
- corrections, voids, resends and handovers.

`/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`.
